      "statusChangeNewStatus": "needs more information",
      "value": "The original avatar `avtr_4e9fc63a-a81d-4a1c-920c-664c7344b092` and repro avatar `avtr_03cda2e5-1727-4d41-8712-9c4b95c52506` appear to have additional differences beyond one being converted to VRChat constraints. The game object Raycast contains a scale constraint in both cases, but the original avatar has it scale constrained to a prefab that keeps its lossy scale at (1, 1, 1), while the repro avatar is using a scale constraint with no sources and Freeze To World enabled. This results in a different world scale, which might be contributing to this problem by interfering with FinalIK's initialization.\n\nPlease try updating `avtr_03cda2e5-1727-4d41-8712-9c4b95c52506` so the scale constraint on the Raycast transform targets a prefab with its scale set to (1, 1, 1) as before, with Freeze To World disabled. You might want to back up your project first. I can also see similar cases of constraints changing like this elsewhere on the avatar that you might want to address in the same way, for example the world parent constraint containing the explosion effect.\n\nPlease let us know if the above addresses the problem for you. Thanks!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
