  "details": "1 - Load this avatar : avtr_4e9fc63a-a81d-4a1c-920c-664c7344b092 and gather at least 1 other person.\n\n2 - Navigate to expressions and into \"Powers\" then toggle \"Armageddon\".\n\n3 - This will trigger an explosion 10 units forward that places itself in world space using the old world constraint and a FinalIK grounder pointing down to place itself on the ground.\n\nNote : This is the expected behavior, the avatar has NOT been converted to the new constraints\n\n4 - Load this avatar : avtr_03cda2e5-1727-4d41-8712-9c4b95c52506 \n\n5  - Navigate to expressions and into \"Powers\" then toggle \"Armageddon\".\n\n6 - Notice how now the explosion is nowhere to be seen on the floor but instead spawns around 500 units below the floor. \n\n7 - If using \"Wing toggle\" located in \"Powers\" -> \"Angel Wings\" to fly upwards (by jumping repeatedly), then toggling \"Armageddon\" now the remote user might see it SOMETIMES behave correctly while it is still broken for you\n\nNote 2 : This is the problematic behavior, both avatar have the EXACT same setup for this specific animation (other things on the avatars differ but do not interact with it in any way and never have before). This is the avatar that has been converted to the new constraints  in unity",
